{"module":"banking","voice":"male","duration":157.9,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Banking, insurance and taxes","start":0.0,"end":2.41,"words":[[0.06,0.59],[0.85,1.53],[1.53,1.76],[1.76,2.21]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The history of wealth is covered in its own module.","start":3.21,"end":6.9,"words":[[3.25,3.42],[3.42,4.01],[4.01,4.17],[4.17,4.51],[4.51,4.67],[4.67,5.09],[5.09,5.26],[5.26,5.51],[5.51,5.76],[5.76,6.34]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This one is about today: the ordinary financial systems where race still changes the price.","start":7.25,"end":13.76,"words":[[7.3,7.53],[7.53,7.76],[7.76,7.92],[7.92,8.3],[8.3,8.77],[9.04,9.2],[9.2,9.74],[9.74,10.44],[10.44,10.98],[10.98,11.21],[11.21,11.52],[11.52,11.83],[11.83,12.53],[12.53,12.69],[12.69,13.15]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Who gets a bank","start":14.11,"end":15.47,"words":[[14.15,14.34],[14.34,14.73],[14.73,14.93],[14.93,15.32]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In the FDIC's 2021 survey, about 11% of Black households had no bank account, compared with about 2% of white households.","start":16.17,"end":26.87,"words":[[16.22,16.38],[16.38,16.53],[16.53,16.93],[16.93,18.12],[18.12,18.6],[18.87,19.27],[19.27,20.22],[20.22,20.38],[20.38,20.7],[20.7,21.49],[21.49,21.73],[21.73,21.97],[21.97,22.28],[22.28,22.84],[23.11,23.67],[23.67,23.91],[23.91,24.3],[24.3,24.94],[24.94,25.1],[25.1,25.41],[25.41,26.29]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Without one, families pay more for check cashing and short-term loans.","start":27.22,"end":32.1,"words":[[27.27,27.76],[27.76,28.09],[28.38,28.95],[28.95,29.2],[29.2,29.36],[29.36,29.52],[29.52,29.85],[29.85,30.26],[30.26,30.51],[30.51,31.0],[31.0,31.49]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Black-owned banks and community development credit unions serve many of these neighborhoods; only about 20 Black-owned banks remain.","start":32.45,"end":40.83,"words":[[32.49,33.05],[33.05,33.4],[33.4,33.62],[33.62,34.25],[34.25,35.03],[35.03,35.45],[35.45,35.95],[35.95,36.16],[36.16,36.44],[36.44,36.58],[36.58,36.79],[36.79,37.5],[37.75,38.1],[38.1,38.45],[38.45,38.87],[38.87,39.44],[39.44,39.79],[39.79,40.29]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Mortgages","start":41.73,"end":42.73,"words":[[41.78,42.5]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Black and Latino borrowers pay higher mortgage rates than comparable white borrowers (Bartlett et al., 2022).","start":43.43,"end":52.15,"words":[[43.48,43.83],[43.83,44.09],[44.09,44.71],[44.71,45.32],[45.32,45.59],[45.59,45.94],[45.94,46.46],[46.46,46.9],[46.9,47.17],[47.17,48.04],[48.04,48.39],[48.39,49.01],[49.01,49.54],[49.54,49.71],[49.71,49.98],[50.28,51.6]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Lenders have paid large settlements over steering minority borrowers into costlier loans, including Countrywide (2011) and Wells Fargo (2012).","start":52.5,"end":63.11,"words":[[52.55,53.0],[53.0,53.22],[53.22,53.53],[53.53,53.83],[53.83,54.58],[54.58,54.88],[54.88,55.41],[55.41,56.09],[56.09,56.61],[56.61,56.91],[56.91,57.52],[57.52,57.97],[58.23,58.83],[58.83,59.59],[59.59,60.57],[60.83,61.06],[61.06,61.36],[61.36,61.73],[61.73,62.64]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Are approval algorithms biased?","start":64.01,"end":66.39,"words":[[64.07,64.14],[64.14,64.64],[64.64,65.34],[65.34,65.84]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A 2021 analysis by The Markup of public mortgage data found lenders were about 80% more likely to deny Black applicants than similar white applicants.","start":67.09,"end":77.55,"words":[[67.14,67.29],[67.29,68.39],[68.39,68.99],[68.99,69.21],[69.21,69.36],[69.36,69.72],[69.72,69.87],[69.87,70.32],[70.32,70.76],[70.76,71.13],[71.13,71.5],[71.5,71.94],[71.94,72.09],[72.09,72.46],[72.46,73.2],[73.2,73.35],[73.35,73.79],[73.79,73.94],[73.94,74.31],[74.31,74.6],[74.6,75.27],[75.27,75.49],[75.49,75.93],[75.93,76.23],[76.23,76.97]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The lending industry disputed it, noting the public data lacks credit scores.","start":77.9,"end":82.71,"words":[[77.95,78.08],[78.08,78.48],[78.48,79.0],[79.0,79.6],[79.6,79.8],[80.03,80.42],[80.42,80.55],[80.55,80.95],[80.95,81.28],[81.28,81.54],[81.54,81.94],[81.94,82.27]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Regulators and researchers continue to debate how much of the gap comes from bias in models versus differences in credit histories that themselves reflect past discrimination.","start":83.06,"end":93.84,"words":[[83.11,83.9],[83.9,84.12],[84.12,84.7],[84.7,85.28],[85.28,85.43],[85.43,85.86],[85.86,86.08],[86.08,86.37],[86.37,86.52],[86.52,86.66],[86.66,86.88],[86.88,87.17],[87.17,87.46],[87.46,87.82],[87.82,87.97],[87.97,88.41],[88.41,88.77],[88.77,89.42],[89.42,89.57],[89.57,90.0],[90.0,90.58],[90.58,90.8],[90.8,91.38],[91.38,91.89],[91.89,92.18],[92.18,93.27]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Appraisals, insurance and property taxes","start":94.74,"end":98.28,"words":[[94.79,95.65],[95.95,96.72],[96.72,96.97],[96.97,97.57],[97.57,98.08]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Homes in Black neighborhoods are appraised lower (see “Is racism over?”).","start":98.98,"end":103.67,"words":[[99.03,99.44],[99.44,99.61],[99.61,99.94],[99.94,100.68],[100.68,100.76],[100.76,101.34],[101.34,101.67],[101.67,101.83],[101.83,102.0],[102.0,102.66],[102.66,103.07]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A 2017 investigation by ProPublica and Consumer Reports found some insurers charged car insurance premiums as much as 30% higher in minority neighborhoods than in white neighborhoods with similar accident risk.","start":104.02,"end":119.98,"words":[[104.07,104.24],[104.24,105.42],[105.42,106.51],[106.51,106.77],[106.77,107.69],[107.69,107.94],[107.94,108.53],[108.53,109.04],[109.04,109.46],[109.46,109.71],[109.71,110.38],[110.38,110.89],[110.89,111.06],[111.06,111.81],[111.81,112.49],[112.49,112.66],[112.66,112.99],[112.99,113.16],[113.16,114.0],[114.0,114.34],[114.34,114.51],[114.51,115.26],[115.26,116.02],[116.02,116.27],[116.27,116.44],[116.44,116.78],[116.78,117.54],[117.54,117.79],[117.79,118.29],[118.29,118.97],[118.97,119.39]]},{"el":"s3","text":"And a 2022 study found Black and Hispanic homeowners pay about 10–13% more in property taxes than white homeowners with the same tax rate, because assessors overvalue cheaper homes relative to their sale prices.","start":120.33,"end":135.85,"words":[[120.38,120.62],[120.62,120.78],[120.78,121.91],[121.91,122.31],[122.31,122.71],[122.71,123.03],[123.03,123.28],[123.28,123.92],[123.92,124.64],[124.64,124.89],[124.89,125.29],[125.29,126.58],[126.58,126.74],[126.74,126.9],[126.9,127.46],[127.46,127.95],[127.95,128.19],[128.19,128.51],[128.51,129.24],[129.24,129.48],[129.48,129.64],[129.64,129.96],[129.96,130.28],[130.28,130.69],[130.97,131.37],[131.37,131.85],[131.85,132.58],[132.58,132.98],[132.98,133.38],[133.38,133.95],[133.95,134.11],[134.11,134.35],[134.35,134.67],[134.67,135.32]]},{"el":"h4","text":"What helps","start":136.75,"end":137.72,"words":[[136.8,137.06],[137.06,137.51]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Bank with Black-owned banks and community lenders, challenge low appraisals with comparable sales, appeal property assessments (free help is often available), and support enforcement of fair lending laws.","start":138.42,"end":151.76,"words":[[138.47,138.78],[138.78,139.02],[139.02,139.64],[139.64,140.03],[140.03,140.26],[140.26,140.96],[140.96,141.5],[141.77,142.4],[142.4,142.63],[142.63,143.33],[143.33,143.56],[143.56,144.34],[144.34,144.8],[145.08,145.39],[145.39,145.93],[145.93,146.63],[146.63,146.86],[146.86,147.17],[147.17,147.33],[147.33,147.64],[147.64,148.42],[148.69,148.92],[148.92,149.31],[149.31,150.01],[150.01,150.16],[150.16,150.4],[150.4,150.86],[150.86,151.17]]},{"el":"s4","text":"The quests “Bank with the community” and “Teach a money workshop” put this into practice.","start":152.11,"end":156.98,"words":[[152.15,152.29],[152.29,152.7],[152.7,152.97],[152.97,153.17],[153.17,153.31],[153.31,153.92],[153.92,154.13],[154.13,154.4],[154.4,154.54],[154.54,154.81],[154.81,155.22],[155.22,155.42],[155.42,155.62],[155.62,155.9],[155.9,156.44]]}]}